WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.370
<i>The antics of my classmate Hanadori 
Kabuto-kun are endlessly annoying.</i>

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.950
<i>But I, Koyuki Seri,</i>

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.680
<i>have challenged myself to never call 
him out, no matter what he does.</i>

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.430
<i>He claims he's the knight of 
light and darkness, Sturmhut,</i>

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.470
<i>who reincarnated into this world 
and battles evil in secret,</i>

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.750
<i>and when his right eye awakens,</i>

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.840
<i>he loses control and becomes the dark 
god of destruction, Miguel Whatever.</i>

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.700
<i>He just lives out this bizarre 
adventure in his own head.</i>

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.870
<i>I was completely humiliated last time,</i>

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.760
<i>and it's all Hanadori-kun's fault.</i>

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.700
<i>Somebody, please do something about him...</i>

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:57.390
<b>A Destructive God Sits Next to Me</b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.940
<b><i>Counseling Room</i></b>

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:15.230
<b><i>Delusion 2</i></b>

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:15.890
Koyuki...

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.620
I'm hungry. Mind if I eat?

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.080
Are you that uninterested in hearing
 what your students have to say?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.920
Hey, don't doubt your teachers.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.680
Stop chewing already!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.270
Say, Koyuki...

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.210
Got any of that stuff? You know...

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.330
The stuff you season rice with.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.780
Rice seasoning!

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.050
You said it yourself! 
Are you doing this on purpose?!

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.620
Well? You got any?

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.860
Of course I don't have any!

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.840
Have you ever had a student here first thing
 in the morning with rice seasoning?!

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.060
Man, you're sure quick to react.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.290
Because you're not listening!

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.480
Now, if only you'd be more 
like that with Hanadori...

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.940
If you don't get something, 
say, "I don't get it!"

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.330
If he's being weird, say, 
"What's wrong with you?"

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.670
That's what we call communication.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.880
I don't want to get involved with him.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.300
But he just won't leave me alone.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.900
Also, I don't yell like that.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.380
Koyuki...

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.460
Have you heard the saying
"birds of a feather"?

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.940
I'll destroy you.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.900
"Birds of a feather flock together."

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.820
It means similar people stick together.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.260
I know what it means!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.350
But I'm nothing like Hanadori-kun!

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.980
Why do I have to explain that?!

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.240
Hanadori's been like that ever
since the first day of school.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.980
For his class introduction, he said,

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.880
"So this is to be my next trial? Not bad."

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.040
Or something.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.200
Why didn't you give him detention?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.660
Kids your age all need something
 to protect yourselves.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:53.010
You want to avoid Hanadori because
 you're trying to protect something, right?

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.310
<i>Protect something? No.</i>

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.760
Forgive my rudeness earlier, Gestöber.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.830
I can't believe you made it past
 my psychic eye, the Hunter Sensor,

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.640
and got behind me.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.350
Your powers are impressive.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:16.480
The Hierophant of Ice's ability, Stealthy Ninja 
Blizzardwalk, is truly a sight to behold.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.200
<i>My skill's name is so stupid!
Why am I a ninja now?</i>

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.660
But it's all clear to me now.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.670
You have the power to save the world.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.150
Gestöber,

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.420
make a pact with me and
become the light of knights!

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.380
<i>Stop ripping off that phrase! 
I know I've heard it before!</i>

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.220
<i>And if you must use it, don't mess with it!</i>

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.350
<i>What does a Hierophant 
of Ice even do, anyway?</i>

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.430
<i>If this were an RPG, I definitely
wouldn't be the main character, right?</i>

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.910
You could be my right-hand man.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.910
Don't miss this opportunity.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.580
<i>I don't know what it is you're selling,</i>

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.910
<i>but if I buy it, I'll spend the 
rest of my life paying for it.</i>

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.010
<i>I'm not getting anywhere, am I?</i>

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:58.440
<i>I'll just have to be harsh and push him away.</i>

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.660
You're bothering me.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.990
Never talk to me again.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.860
<i>If I can make it clear I don't like him,
he should get the hint.</i>

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.330
<i>I don't want to be a jerk, but—</i>

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.310
Swoon!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:18.170
<b>Tremble</b>

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:18.170
<b>Tremble</b>

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.170
<b>Tremble</b>

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.080
<i>Don't swoon at that!</i>

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.170
Wow, Gestöber.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.780
I knew you had the potential 
to change the world.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.540
<i>It's no use. He's not listening.</i>

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.510
That piercing gaze that
 betrays your inner animal...

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.520
I can see why they call you "Pointy Icicle."

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.960
<i>Another stupid name!</i>

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.680
<i>Put some thought into these!</i>

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.440
<i>That's how Hanadori-kun is, 
and I still have no idea what he's after.</i>

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.280
<i>He probably just wants to feel special.</i>

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.920
<i>And I just don't want to get involved with him.</i>

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.310
<i>That's all.</i>

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:48.700
But why?

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.000
Why don't you want to get
involved with Hanadori-kun?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.910
It's kind of fun!

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.160
<i>That scared me! When did he get here?</i>

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.620
<i>And how can he read my mind?</i>

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:02.820
<i>I don't know if Tsukimiya-kun
is Hanadori-kun's friend or what,</i>

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.590
<i>but I should keep my distance from him, too!</i>

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.400
So why? Why?

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.050
Because you'll stand out?
Because you want to focus on school?

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.580
Th-Those are good reasons, aren't they?

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.520
I see...

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.880
Then how did it feel when 
you realized that the guy

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.730
you were trying to avoid 
hadn't even noticed you?

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.960
Well? Well? How did that feel?

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.190
<i>Is he the devil?</i>

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.500
<i>Stop it! Don't bring that up!</i>

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.530
Huh? Huh? Huh? How'd it feel?

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.840
<i>Hanadori-kun wasn't trying 
to be mean, but you were!</i>

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.700
You were standing right there in front of him,

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.840
and he just completely ignored you!

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.590
<i>I'm experiencing incredible mental distress!</i>

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.710
So, so? How'd it feel?

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.060
Hey, Gestöber.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.170
Let's go save the world from a rift.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.720
<i>Say what?</i>

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:57.340
I see. So in this world, you call it 
the disciplinary committee?

00:06:53.430 --> 00:07:04.150
<b>Mitoya High School</b>

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.540
We have a duty to wipe out
 evil wherever we find it...

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.130
Plus that.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.720
He just called you "that," Cerberus!

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.610
<i>Why am I here?</i>

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:18.620
<b>Disciplinary Committee</b>

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.560
The disciplinary committee...

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.020
A lapse in the dress code
is a lapse in discipline,

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.720
as well as a lapse in morality.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:17.620
As the knight of light and darkness, 
correcting that is my sworn duty.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.700
So be it.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:23.280
<i>Hanadori-kun, you break
 all kinds of school rules.</i>

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.780
<i>You just wanted to wear the arm band?!</i>

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.610
<i>Okay, okay... Looking good.</i>

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:38.420
<i>I want to get back to class already and study.</i>

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.580
<i>Problem detected!</i>

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.280
<i>That's not even close to our uniform,
not to mention her boots and bag...</i>

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.980
<i>I guess we have to say something to her.</i>

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.040
<i>You do it, Hanadori-kun.</i>

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.860
<i>The heck? What happened to saving the world?</i>

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:57.510
<b>Fidget</b>

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.140
<b>Fidget</b>

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:58.760
<b>Fidget</b>

00:07:58.760 --> 00:07:59.330
<b>Fidget</b>

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.750
<b>S
c
r
a
t
c
h

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.160
Oh, right!

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.990
I've gotta go buy food for Cerberus!

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.410
<i>Hey, wait, shy boy!</i>

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:19.640
<i>What? The knight of light and darkness 
can't even talk to a girl?</i>

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.910
<i>And he's running away?</i>

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.060
<i>Just how scared is he?</i>

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.000
No, Cerberus!

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.240
If you run out into the street and get hit—

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.420
<i>The knight got hit!</i>

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.320
<i>Wh-What even happened?</i>

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.160
<b>Ha
ha
ha
ha
ha</b>

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.160
<i>Are you okay, Hanadori-kun?</i>

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.000
Who's this?

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.600
Oh, you're that second-year, Hanadori Kabuto.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.020
Was slamming into me 
your way of saying hello?

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.590
N-No, um...

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:49.740
That's Gorio the Gorilla,

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:53.470
the legendary leader who 
brought back the school gang!

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.480
<i>What?</i>

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.480
<i>Is everybody in this school like him?</i>

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:00.140
Is that how the disciplinary
committee greets people now?

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:00.660
<b>Disciplinary Committee</b>

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.850
<i>He hid it!</i>

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.090
Hey, Hanadori...
Why'd you cover up your arm?

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:07.560
Move your hand.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.910
Just an old wound acting up. That's all.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.810
I've heard about you.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:17.690
They say if your eyepatch comes off,
something interesting happens, right?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:18.970
N-No!

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.240
<i>So he's gotten a reputation...</i>

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:24.080
Stop! Stop it! Don't! You can't! Stop!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.100
<i>But really, something annoying
will happen, so just leave it.</i>

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.370
Let's see it!

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.070
Are you trying to piss me off?!

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:36.270
<i>You think you can just hide it with your hand?</i>

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.480
S-Stop!

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:39.730
<i>Can Miguel Whatever, the dark god 
of destruction, be stopped so easily?</i>

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.100
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.360
Unhand me!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.290
<i>Hanadori-kun can't even keep
his own character straight.</i>

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.390
<i>And if he can't...</i>

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.360
Don't think you'll get away
with your evil deeds!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.040
<i>He should just act normal.</i>

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.550
Hey, let me go! I mean it!

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.840
<i>Then nobody will bug him.</i>

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.060
<i>Just apologize and—</i>

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.820
Don't mess with me, Hanadori...

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.780
Or I'll send this mutt flying!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:09:59.960
Cerberus!

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.430
D-Don't do it!

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:02.940
Don't hurt Cerberus!

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:05.230
He's too important to me!

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.580
Just don't hurt him!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.650
Please, spare him!

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.050
Take it out on me instead! Me!

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.740
I'll pay you.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.720
Don't try to solve this with money!

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.660
I thought you were going
to let him punch you!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.280
Where the hell is Miguel?!

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.730
That money is for Cerberus's food!

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.840
Thanks for waking me up.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:37.040
You truly are as keen and hard as ice,

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.020
but your passion burns like frostbite.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.530
You are my truest friend, Gestöber!

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:45.000
<i>Oh, crap... I blurted that out loud.</i>

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.960
<b><i>Counseling Room</i></b>

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.690
Why did you hit Hanadori?

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.920
I was just so mad...

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.760
<i>I've gone and done it again.</i>

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:58.150
<i>I swore I wouldn't react to him, 
but I slipped up.</i>

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.460
<i>In front of everyone, no less...</i>

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.380
Koyuki...

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.480
We often hate people who are too much like us.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:04.600
Please stop.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.500
You see, sometimes we hate people...

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:10.190
Because if opposites attract,
 then like poles repel?

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.820
Please stop. It's not like that.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.280
I just want to live a normal life, 
but he won't let me—

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:19.420
Seri-kun likes to think of himself as special,

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:21.870
which is why he says he wants to "be normal."

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:25.000
That's what makes him like Hanadori, I bet.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.040
<i>How humiliating...</i>

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.590
That's what makes you like Hanadori.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:31.040
Don't say it twice!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:38.710
RIP
Koyuki

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:35.580
<i>I, Koyuki Seri, haven't just lost to myself
 over not reacting to Hanadori-kun.</i>

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:38.710
RIP
Koyuki

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:38.710
RIP
Koyuki

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.710
RIP
Koyuki

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.710
RIP
Koyuki

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:37.980
<i>Now I've lost to Tsukimiya-kun, too.</i>

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:40.970
Koyuki!

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.740
Got any plans for summer vacation?

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:44.550
Do you?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.420
Me? I'm booked.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:51.520
Every girl wants to go see fireworks
and hit up the beach for a date, you know?

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:54.640
I'm gonna be so busy! Super busy!

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:57.620
But I know you'll be lonely all by yourself...

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.940
<b>Heart-Pounding Memorial</b>

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:58.750
So here!

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.950
You should get a girlfriend, too!

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.420
Just kidding!

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.620
Haha!

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:08.370
Have fun trying to get with a 2D girl!

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.240
Koyuki's learned to deliver
his insults with a smile...

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.080
I thought he'd just hit me 
like he usually does.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.950
Did something happen?

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:21.760
You were hoping he'd hit you?

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:25.360
<i>So much has happened that 
I felt like a dead man, but...</i>

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:30.020
Um, Koyuki-kun, you're
so much more cheerful lately.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.480
You were hard to approach before 
since you always seemed angry...

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.880
But I've always wanted to try talking to you!

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.860
<i>The girl I like, Sumiso Kotoko, said that to me!</i>

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.330
<i>I can't believe it!</i>

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.400
<i>Plus, it's almost summer break!</i>

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.040
<i>Just thinking about how I won't
have to see either of them</i>

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:52.960
<i>has made my whole world brighter!</i>

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.500
Koyuki-kun!

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:57.160
Can I have your phone number?

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.210
Sure!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.810
Here you go.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.680
I'll send you my number 
and my email later, okay?

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:04.320
Sure! Thanks.

